Thursday Update
* Trade Alert: Sold TSM calls for 99% gain; buy CCL and TSM calls* Stocks f=
lash higher on optimism for fiscal spending and improved economic dataStock=
s are blasting higher Thursday as market participants anticipate the approv=
al of a higher stimulus payment following this week's Democratic victory in=
 Georgia's Senate runoff, while violent incidents in DC were shrugged off a=
s immaterial to corporate earnings."Democrats picked up both Georgia Senate=
 seats, paving the way for Biden to implement his agenda more broadly. This=
 should result in additional stimulus, including the expansion of payments =
to individuals," Credit Suisse said in a report.Analysts at Credit Suisse a=
nd Pantheon Macroeconomics said that the Democratic control is not likely t=
o translate into unbridled spending."Fiscal policy will be looser with Demo=
crats controlling the Senate, but don't expect an explosion," said Ian Shep=
herdson, chief economist at Pantheon Macroeconomics. He noted that Democrat=
s would need in the Senate least 60 votes for fiscal measures.Chaotic event=
s Wednesday afternoon inside the Capitol were likely to be "no more than a =
temporary distraction," according to a report from Commerzbank, which added=
 that traders were positioning for a path forward for further fiscal stimul=
us spending in the US.Through 2:30 pm ET, the Dow was up 220 pts or 0.7% wh=
ile the S&amp;P 500 rose 1.4%, the Nasdaq 100 was up 2.3% and the Smallcap =
600 was up 5.5%.On the Standard &amp; Poor's 500 financials and information=
 technology were leading gains, with rises of 2.2% and 1.9%, respectively. =
Energy was 1.2% higher with crude oil prices little changed .In company new=
s, 3D Systems (DDD) surged 35% after the 3D printer makers said that it exp=
ects fourth quarter revenue to be as much as $176 million. =E2=80=A6 Bed Ba=
th &amp; Beyond (BBBY) fell 8.2% after it reported fiscal third quarter adj=
usted earnings of $0.08 per share. Analysts polled by Capital IQ had projec=
ted adjusted EPS of $0.20. =E2=80=A6 Ryanair (RYAAY) fell 2.4% after the lo=
w-cost carrier said it expects to significantly cut its flight schedule thr=
ough March due to newly announced lockdowns in Ireland, the UK, and other E=
uropean Union countries. ... Plug Power (PLUG) rose 30% after South Korea's=
 SK Group planned to make a $1.5 billion strategic investment in the compan=
y.Portfolio: We sold second half of TSM calls for 99% gain today at the ope=
n, which is awesome. Sold MS and DD calls yesterday for gains of 29% to 80%=
, very cool. =E2=80=A6 One new idea today plus another stab at TSM calls vi=
a a different strike.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONSTaiwan Semiconductor (TSM) Jan=
uary $110 calls-- Symbol: TSM210115C00110000-- Bought on Jan 4 at $4.60-- S=
old first half at $6.30 on Jan 5 for a 37% gain!-- Sold second half at the =
$9.15 open for gain of 98.9%!&nbsp;-- Cancel stop. This trade is complete.*=
&nbsp;NEW RECOMMENDATIONS.Carnival Corp. (CCL) January 15 calls-- Symbol: C=
